Reason: After insertion, size should be one greater than return value.--------------------Sure, so the following C# code that reads the input code and outputs an Assert Statement when it encounters a comment starting with `@@@`.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;
using System.Linq;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        var csharpCode = System.IO.File.ReadAllText("InputFileName.cs"); // Read the csharp code from the file

        /*
        You have to remove all the comments from the C# code using Regular Expression
        
        Because "//" and "/*...*/" are two types of comments in C#.
        So we first remove single line comments and then multi line comments.
        */

        csharpCode = Regex.Replace(csharpCode, @"//.*?\n", "\n");
        csharpCode = Regex.Replace(csharpCode, @"/\*(.|\n)*?\*/", "");

        /* Now find matches for comments starting with `@@@`*/

        var match = Regex.Matches(csharpCode, @"//\s*@@@(.*)");

        foreach (Match m in match)
        {
            if (m.Success)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Debug.Assert({m.Value.TrimStart('/', ' ', '\n')});");
            }
        }
    }
}
```
Please replace `"InputFileName.cs"` with your file path that contains your C# code. And this code will print all assertions found in your code. 

